// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SecurityCodes 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P129713494" "Security Codes"
// DetailString :
"P1841788284" "This file contains some security codes. You're not sure why Hero 1 would hide this info in the time capsule or why Mueller would want it, but recovering them pays well and that's all that really matters."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Payday 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3430740081" "Big Payoff from Mueller"
// DetailString :
"P2054444866" "Mueller must have really wanted those security codes, because he was really willing to pay for them! That was some payday for what was a pretty simple job. Hopefully, he'll have more jobs like that for you in the future."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DimensionalExperiments 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3024014089" "Dimensional Experiments"
// DetailString :
"P2414588007" "These computer files detail the various experiments performed by 5th Column scientists on the subject of alternate dimensions and paranormal energy. Your first read of the documents reveal that they are working on some kind of device to help Reichsman, but the details are buried under a lot of scientific mumbo-jumbo. It's going to take a detailed study to get to the bottom of exactly what they're attempting. "

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Tough 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2145875341" "Invincible Reichsman"
// DetailString :
"P778442054" "When you faced Reichsman in Boomtown he seemed to be unbeatable. You're going to need to figure out why he's so tough and find a way to counter it if you're going to have a chance at taking him down. And, somehow, you know you're going to have to be the one who deals with this guy."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DimensionalPower 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P140173264" "Empowering Reichsman"
// DetailString :
"P2332042137" "According to this information, Reichsman is empowering himself by stealing the energy from his counterparts, those other Marcus Coles from the different dimensions. The confluence of this energy makes him effectively unstoppable. From reading through the files, you know that Reichsman's got some kind of big machine back on Earth Prime that's holding those alternate Reichsmans and siphoning the energy to him.<br><br>The machine like it is very well defending. And you know you can't stand up against Reichsman in his current empowered state. But you think you can use his machine on you and your crew, to give you the edge you need to take him down.<br><br>If you can get a few very powerful beings into the machine, you can use it to give you some defenses and counters to Reichsman's new powers. Maybe you can convince Lord Recluse to lend you his lieutenants for this. You might just get away with it... if you don't tell him why you need them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeOneClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2534391363" "Thus Spoke The Reichsman"
// DetailString :
"P1974307549" "Barracuda introduced you to Roderick Mueller, an Arachnos agent, who had a sweet little job for you. He hired you to hit City Hall in Atlas Park and steal some computer file out of the Omega Force's Time Capsule. You fought your way through the defenders with relative ease and got the goods to Muller for a really good payoff. It's jobs like this that make you remember why you like doing what you do."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeTwoClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2242776737" "Barracuda introduced you to Roderick Mueller, an Arachnos agent, who had a sweet little job for you. He hired you to hit City Hall in Atlas Park and steal some computer file out of the Omega Force's Time Capsule. You fought your way through the defenders with relative ease and got the goods to Muller for a really good payoff. It's jobs like this that make you remember why you like doing what you do.<br><br>Mueller had another one of those high-paying jobs for you. It seemed the file you stole had the security codes to an old Freedom Phalanx base under Boomtown, and Mueller wanted some muscle to escort him inside so he could use those codes to recover something. With the promise of a big payoff, you overcame the guards, beat up Numina, and got Mueller to the containment area he was trying to reach. And that's when things went bad. The containment area held Reichsman -- some kind of whacked out twisted 5th Column version of Statesman -- and the next thing you knew Mueller was toasted, your payday was shot, and you were waking up in a 5th Column jail cell. You busted out of there and found and trashed Schadenfreude, some 5th Column baddie who was calling the shots in the base. You got out of there, but not before stealing some information that showed the 5th Column was back and up to something big."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeThreeClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P4164893709" "Roderick Mueller hired you to steal some security codes from City Hall in Atlas Park and then to escort him to use them in a Freedom Phalanx base in Boomtown. That's when things went bad and you ended up with no payday and Reichsman freed from where he'd be imprisoned for a long while.<br><br>Lord Recluse was <color red>not</color> amused by this, especially when the 5th Column reappeared to invade Boomtown. Figuring it was only a matter of time before they set their eyes on the Rogue Isles, Lord Recluse sent you to Boomtown to 'clean up your mess' and stop the invasion. Knowing what was good for you, you headed over there only to find that the invasion was being spearheaded by Reichsman, who was far too powerful for you to defeat. It was like he was supercharged or something. You activated an old Freedom Phalanx signal as a distraction and managed to escape from Boomtown. Now you need to figure out how to stop someone who's seemingly unstoppable."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - EpisodeFourClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P431608315" "After Roderick Mueller's job went awry and you freed Reichsman from imprisonment, Lord Recluse sent you to Boomtown to 'clean up your mess' and get rid of the 5th Column invasion. You followed orders, but found that Reichsman had been supercharged and was virtually unstoppable. You retreated to come up with another approach.<br><br>Acting on information you recovered during the whole freeing Reichsman debacle, you used the Destiny Portal to travel to Axis Earth, Reichsman's home dimension. Once there, you wasted no time in beating the location of a Axis base out of some soldiers and went there to see what you could find out. The base's commander had some access codes that got you into the computer system. The computer had some interesting information on a machine that Reichsman was using to transfer energy from alternate Reichsman into him, effectively super-charging him. That information was what you needed to come up with a plan to stop the 5th Column leader."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL9_ThusSpokeTheReichsman_StrikeForce 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3764680220" "Reichsman's Helmet"
// tDetailString :
"P3303477195" "This helmet is a souvenir of a little caper you like to call<br><br>Thus Spoke The Reichsman<br><br>It all started when Barracuda tipped you to a job that Roderick Mueller wanted done. It was a simple theft, in and out with a big payday at the end. But it didn't stay that easy.<br><br>After Roderick Mueller's second job went awry and you freed Reichsman from imprisonment, Lord Recluse sent you to Boomtown to 'clean up your mess' and get rid of the 5th Column invasion. You followed orders, but found that Reichsman had been supercharged and was virtually unstoppable. You retreated to come up with another approach.<br><br>Acting on information you recovered during the whole freeing Reichsman debacle, you used the Destiny Portal to travel to Axis Earth, Reichsman's home dimension. Once there, you found some interesting information that Reichsman was using a machine to transfer energy from alternate Reichsmans into him, effectively super-charging him. That information was what you needed to come up with a plan to stop the 5th Column leader.<br><br>You went back to Recluse and negotiated the loan of Ghost Widow, Captain Mako, Scirocco, and Black Scorpion to help you in fighting Reichsman. You didn't tell Recluse that you were going to pound his lieutenants and then shove them into the empowering machine to give you the edge you needed to beat Reichsman. Recluse caught on a little too late, arriving just in time to get his head handed to him by Reichsman. You seized the opportunity to negotiate a fat payday -- and forgiveness -- from him and then went off to finish off Reichsman. You sealed the deal and can walk with your head held high, knowing that you did something Recluse couldn't -- you took down Reichsman."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission_1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P490923054" "I got an opportunity for you, {HeroName}, and I'm sure you're gonna help me out. This squint, Roderick Mueller, has a job he needs a little help with, and you're gonna give him the help he needs. Don't worry; he's gonna take good care of you for your help, and you're gonna take good care of me for cluing you in on this opportunity.<br><br>Mueller's got a line on some info he needs. The only problem is, that info is hidden in that Omega Team time capsule they got there.<color orange> The capsule's been moved to under City Hall, so this Mueller wants you to go in there and swipe that info.</color><br><br>Whadda say, {HeroName}? You in?"
// AcceptString :
"P2064558173" "Help Mueller"
// SendOffString :
"P1221090168" "OK, Mueller's got a flyer waitin' that will bring you and your crew to Paragon City. <color orange>It's a simple job, get in, get the info, get out.</color><br><br>Once you finish whatever his deal is, make sure you come back and let me in on a piece of the action. You'll do that, if you know what's good for you. Otherwise... Well, there ain't gonna be an otherwise, is there?"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1064608238" "Rob City Hall"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P929458157" "The Arachnos flyer is waiting for you outside of Grandville. Head to Atlas Park and steal that file from the time capsule!"
// TaskTitle :
"P2020630090" "<color deepskyblue>Thus Spoke The Reichsman</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2153175688" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: Things Thought Forgotten</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2881993139" "They probably thought that City Hall was a good place to hold something valuable. Well, you're about to prove that assumption wrong."

